# L §6.4 (tally 2.1.6, P29 on T's SR-T1 of #75): load sees that an instance of a scenario's move books before D only
# where it sees the instance's day and its existence; a move with a `when` exists where the when holds, at run. top's
# when reads an input, so load refuses nothing, and the two instances before 2026-01-01 are left out at run (L §6.4's
# first half). 2.1.6's first refcore (522a715) refused topup at load, LOAD-SCENARIO top books on 2025-12-30; tally
# 2.1.5's answered 15.00 PLN, as household B's k5 copy (forecast's hr5_topup) did. Twin: _days_no_when_refused.
=== base.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-02
  start 2025-12-30
  end 2026-01-05

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input from_day: date

input early: date

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-05)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  from_day = 2026-01-01
  early = 2025-01-01
  opening[konto] = 10.00 PLN at 2025-12-30 start
=== scen.tally
scenario topup over hh
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

move top[d in days]: transfers
  on d
  when d >= early
  leg cash from world to konto amount 1.00 PLN

ask q_top: bal(konto, 2026-01-05) in topup
=== expect q_top
q_top: 15.00 PLN
  world: topup
  unfulfilled: top[2026-01-01]
  left out: top, 2 instances, first 2025-12-30
  cut 2026-01-02
warning: WARN-UNREAD input from_day is read by nothing
